                <pb facs="0621" n="509" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg509"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 23297/1.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Bacon to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-01-29"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">January 29,
                    1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Bacon states that Red Cross remittances to the French Government should be
                    sent through the embassy, and that if there is a preference as to the channel of
                    distribution it should be indicated. For instance, he says, if the French Red
                    Cross is preferred, it should be so indicated, and he adds that this society is
                    well organized, responsible, and efficient.</p>
            </div>
